      "id": "GENUS_OCEANITES",
      "name": "Oceanites",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Small, sooty-brown storm petrels with a conspicuous white rump and pale underwing bar. They patter on the water surface with a distinctive fluttering flight, feeding on plankton and small fish. The genus includes Wilson's Storm Petrel, one of the most abundant and widely distributed seabirds on Earth.",
